    {
      "id": "66aaygb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Sound"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Sound is a mechanical longitudinal wave produced by vibrating objects and requires a material medium for propagation.",
        "Human hearing is sensitive to frequencies between 20 Hz and 20,000 Hz (20 kHz).",
        "Speed of sound is maximum in solids, moderate in liquids, minimum in gases, and zero in a vacuum.",
        "An echo requires a minimum distance of 17.2 meters between the sound source and the reflecting surface.",
        "Ultrasound (frequency > 20 kHz) is used in medical imaging, SONAR, and cleaning hard-to-reach industrial parts."
      ],
      "id": "us787a7"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ecqmeyc",
      "content": "• Sound is a form of energy that produces the sensation of hearing."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "exdaiom",
      "content": "• It is produced by vibrating objects."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "60nuby4",
      "content": "• Sound travels through a medium in the form of waves."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "10pgifg",
      "content": "• It cannot travel through vacuum because it requires a material medium."
    },
    {
      "id": "ufyle0m",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Production of Sound"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qqh6ctf",
      "content": "• Sound is produced when an object vibrates."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9xbz5d7",
      "content": "• The vibrating object causes nearby particles of the medium to vibrate."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bq249pg",
      "content": "• These vibrations travel through the medium as sound waves."
    },
    {
      "id": "wu6yn51",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Sound Waves"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0goyqv8",
      "content": "Sound waves are longitudinal waves consisting of compressions and rarefactions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "um35sk2",
      "content": "• Compression – region of high pressure."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nbfl4ek",
      "content": "• Rarefaction – region of low pressure."
    },
    {
      "id": "hygncsr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Characteristics of Sound Waves"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Sound waves are longitudinal mechanical waves that require a material medium for their propagation and cannot travel through a vacuum.",
      "id": "y7peuzq"
    },
    {
